812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Wall Street edges lower","datePublished":"2019-02-26T21:23:21Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T21:23:21Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c7598848534010677b84bcd","articleBody":"Wall Street's three major\nindexes fell slightly after a choppy session as\ninvestors digested mixed economic data and corporate news. Traders said many investors also stayed on the sidelines waiting for clarity on issues such as\nUS-China trade talks. At the close, the Dow Jones was down 0.13% to 26,057.5, while the S&P 500 lost 0.08% to 2,793.8. The Nasdaq dropped 0.07% to 7,549.3.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Container firms told probe is off","datePublished":"2019-02-26T21:13:51Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T21:13:51Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c7594ce8534010677b84bc4","articleBody":"Hapag-Lloyd, the massive German shipping firm, said it has been cleared in a US Department of Justice probe with no charges\nbrought. \"Hapag-Lloyd was informed that the U.S. Department of\nJustice, Antitrust Division is closing its investigation without\ncharges against the company, its affiliates or any other current\nor former employees,\" Reuters quotes a company spokesman as saying. Maersk\n and Mediterranean Shipping Company made similar statements earlier.\n    The investigation could have resulted in fines at a\ntime when the container sector is struggling with slowing global\neconomic growth.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://c.files.bbci.co.uk/vivo/live/images/2019/2/26/e755b5e9-0fa0-4554-985a-13b81e0c9226.jpg","caption":"containers","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":false,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":683}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"'No rush' on US rates decisions","datePublished":"2019-02-26T21:02:15Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T21:02:15Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c75a28f7c432e0681fbdce0","articleBody":"The US central bank, the Federal Reserve, is in \"no\nrush to make a judgement\" about further changes to interest\nrates, its chairman Jerome Powell told a committee of senators. Disappointing data on\nretail sales contrast with\nsteady hiring and wage growth, he said, sending \"conflicting signals\".","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Why delay?","datePublished":"2019-02-26T20:54:19Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T20:54:19Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c7595d4cf24dd06818919a2","articleBody":"France's finance minister says that Britain, if it wants to delay Brexit, will need to be clear as to why it should get one an extension. \"If there is no clarity on the purpose of that extension, I\ndon't see the necessity of that extension, so it is up to the\nBritish government to explain to us if they are asking for an\nextension,\" Bruno Le Maire said after a speech in Dublin on\nTuesday.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://c.files.bbci.co.uk/vivo/live/images/2019/2/26/62e8280f-d415-415e-baa6-30d287b4cf68.jpg","caption":"fin min","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":false,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":682}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Fiat Chrysler jobs cut","datePublished":"2019-02-26T20:27:55Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T20:27:55Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c759e5e7c432e0681fbdcc9","articleBody":"Fiat Chrysler will cut nearly 1,400 jobs at an Illinois\nassembly plant where it builds the Jeep Cherokee, Reuters reports. The firm is cutting one of three shifts\nat the Belvidere Assembly plant starting in May. \n    Earlier it announced it was investing\n$4.5bn in five plants and creating 6,500 jobs in Michigan,\nincluding building a new assembly plant in Detroit.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://c.files.bbci.co.uk/vivo/live/images/2019/2/26/2ec293d8-d427-4f82-84a4-1ace341d8401.jpg","caption":"jeep","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":false,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":697}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Brexit impact assessment","datePublished":"2019-02-26T20:09:06Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T20:09:06Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c759ad08534010677b84bd9","articleBody":"The government has published its assessment of the impact of a no-deal Brexit on business and trade. The report said \"some food prices are likely to increase\" and customs checks could cost business £13bn a year in a no-deal scenario. It also said there was \"little evidence that businesses are preparing in earnest\". But the government said it had undertaken \"significant action\" to prepare for no deal on 29 March.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Dutch bought Air France-KLM stake","datePublished":"2019-02-26T19:49:13Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T19:49:13Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c7598388534010677b84bca","articleBody":"The Netherlands bought a 12.7% stake in Air France-KLM in a bid to strengthen its influence in the airline, the Dutch finance minister said. They want to eventually own the same size stake France does, finance minister Wopke Hoekstra told a press conference in The Hague. France owns 14.3% of the carrier , Delta owns 8.8%, China Eastern 8.8% and employees 3.9%.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://c.files.bbci.co.uk/vivo/live/images/2019/2/26/f6e17b5f-bb74-4748-a9f0-65fb42242125.jpg","caption":"fin min","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":false,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":631}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Emma Thompson made stand over Lasseter hiring","datePublished":"2019-02-26T19:03:11Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T19:03:11Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c75871c7c432e0681fbdc7c","articleBody":"Emma Thompson has revealed she quit an animated project because the company making it had hired John Lasseter. Lasseter was recruited to head Skydance Animation following his departure from Pixar in the wake of claims he sexually harassed female colleagues. In a letter, Thompson questioned the studio \"hiring someone with Mr Lasseter's pattern of misconduct\". The actress had been due to voice a character in Luck, a comedy about how luck affects our daily lives. BBC News has contacted Skydance to request a comment. Read her letter here.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Rail franchise system \"cannot continue\"","datePublished":"2019-02-26T18:43:35Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T18:43:35Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c7587d17c432e0681fbdc80","articleBody":"Britain's rail franchise system no longer delivers clear benefits and cannot continue as it is, says the man leading a review of the network. Keith Williams will say in a speech later the industry is not responding to fast-changing consumer demands. Rail franchising - contracting out passenger services - has drawn heavy criticism, with some contracts failing and customer complaints rising. The rail industry said it accepts that the status quo cannot continue. Full story here.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://c.files.bbci.co.uk/vivo/live/images/2019/2/26/6f3685f2-e3bd-4b28-a4e9-d651002ebfda.jpg","caption":"train","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":false,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":683}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Metro reports profit doubles","datePublished":"2019-02-26T18:01:59Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T18:01:59Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c757f177c432e0681fbdc74","articleBody":"Metro Bank said its 2018 net profit more than doubled to £27m and it says it already has a nice, fat capital buffer. The £350m it wants is to fund growth, it said. So that's, er, good news then? Well, the lender is now under investigation by the Bank of England for that update last month on risky mortgages that sent the shares tanking. It is quite unusual to announce a capital raise six minutes before the end of trading without saying what you plan to do with the money, and then report earnings after hours .","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Alternative ports","datePublished":"2019-02-26T17:47:45Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T17:47:45Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c7568298534010677b84b6d","articleBody":"Here's an interesting map from Bloomberg showing alternative ports businesses may use in case of a no-deal situation.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Hotel Chocolat results 'very strong'","datePublished":"2019-02-26T17:21:02Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T17:21:02Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c74eefa8534010677b84a18","articleBody":"Hotel Cocolat's half year results are \"very strong\" according to an analyst note from investment bank Liberum. It said a 13% increase in revenue to £80.7m \"has been delivered while investment in new markets, new wholesale\npartners, the start of a loyalty scheme and new products have launched in the\nperiod.\"","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://c.files.bbci.co.uk/vivo/live/images/2019/2/26/bcc3f63c-c341-4c47-92f3-9749f33aaf04.jpg","caption":"Hotel Chocolat chocolates","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":false,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":660},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":371}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Tesco warning","datePublished":"2019-02-26T17:15:25Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T17:15:25Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c7572f18534010677b84b81","articleBody":"Another day, another phishing email warning. Here's the police's tips on spotting these emails , but in essence the big giveaway is that the sender's email address doesn't tally with the corporation's web address. Poor English used to be a tell-tale sign, but it is no longer a reliable guide. As ever, if in doubt: report it.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Embraer sale approved","datePublished":"2019-02-26T17:02:29Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T17:02:29Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c75656ccf24dd068189194d","articleBody":"Brazil’s aircraft maker\nEmbraer approved the sale of its commercial jet operation to Boeing. Embraer obtained a victory in\ncourts this morning and overturned a court decision that had suspended the\nvote. Labour unions say the deal is harmful to their interests but 96% of\nshareholders approved the deal. A new company, temporarily\ncalled NewCo, will be created – with 80% ownership by Boeing and 20% by\nEmbraer. Now Boeing and Embraer must seek\napproval from competition bodies in all countries where both firms operate. It\nis expected that NewCo will start operating next year. The tie-up is a response to\nconcentration in the airline business, after rival companies Airbus and\nBombardier also joined forces in 2017.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"http://c.files.bbci.co.uk/1845D/production/_105812499_gettyimages-934658684.jpg","caption":"bank","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":true,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":576}}},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Metro Bank will raise £350m","datePublished":"2019-02-26T16:46:39Z","dateModified":"2019-02-26T16:46:39Z","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907#post_5c756d6e8534010677b84b74","articleBody":"Metro Bank says it will raise £350m in new shares in a late statement . \"In order to accommodate investors in North America and Europe the bank will be announcing its 2018 preliminary results, updated strategy for the medium-term and its 2019 capital plans after the market close today,\" it said.","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/business-47320907","publisher":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"author":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"image":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://c.files.bbci.co.uk/vivo/live/images/2019/2/26/b0de9b62-4ce4-469e-846a-299484ad6808.jpg","caption":"metro","copyrightHolder":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@id":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news#publisher"},"representativeOfPage":false,"width":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":1024},"height":{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QuantitativeValue","unitText":"px","value":684}}}]}</script><div class="lx-c-session-header lx-c-session-header--new-image lx-c-session-header--has-image lx-c-