ications_for_Business_and_Trade_of_a_No_Deal_Exit_on_29_March_2019.pdf" alt="The report ">The report <span class="lx-stream-post-body__external-link gel-icon gel-icon-external-link"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32"><path d="M12 0v5h11.5l-5 5H0v22h22V17.5l-2 2V30H2V12h14.5l-7.8 7.7 3.6 3.6L27 8.5V20h5V0z"></path></svg></span></a>said "some food prices are likely to increase" and customs checks could cost business £13bn a year in a no-deal scenario.</p><p data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.3.0.0:$post_2">It also said there was "little evidence that businesses are preparing in earnest".</p><p data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.3.0.0:$post_3">But the government said it had undertaken "significant action" to prepare for no deal on 29 March.</p><noscript data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.3.0.1"></noscript></div></div><footer class="lx-stream-post__footer" data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.4"><noscript data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.4.0"></noscript><div class="lx-stream-post__footer-share" data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.4.1"><span class="gs-u-vh qa-share-tools-heading" id="share-tools-title-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9" data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.4.1.0">Article share tools</span><ul aria-labelledby="share-tools-title-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9" class="lx-share-tools__items lx-share-tools__items--align-left qa-share-tools" data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.0.0.1.0.$lx-commentary.$lx-commentary.2.0.1.1:$post-5c759ad08534010677b84bd9.0.4.1.1"><li data-reactid=".1fab6pdt5ea.3.